# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO Page Architecture Rules

**Scope:** All repository work — pages, APIs, `src/lib/`, jobs, and any customer-facing behavior. Read the full source doc before implementing.

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-PAGE-ARCHITECTURE-RULES.md`  
**Authority:** Level 4 — page structure and layout.

## Hard requirement

Before designing or implementing any page layout, you **MUST** read the full document and match an approved **page archetype** (list, detail, settings, builder, wizard, dashboard, etc.).

## Non-negotiables

- Complete the **page design worksheet** mentally before pixels — title, primary action, data region, filters, states.
- **Page header** placement, primary CTA hierarchy, and local nav follow archetype rules.
- Handle **loading, empty, error, partial, and success** states on every data surface.
- Do not invent new page anatomy per route — use shared patterns.
- Configuration pages: group related settings; separate dangerous actions.
- Wizards: one primary path forward; preserve progress; clear step labels.

## On conflict

Governance > IA > HCD > this guide > visual design > existing code.
